{"abstract":"The increased popularity of generative AI calls for methods for designers to evaluate their phenomenological qualities. Accuracy or efficiency are not sufficient concepts as the aesthetic qualities of generative models have significant impact on how they work when employed in the real world. I have propose an approach to designing for the reflexive use of generative AI. The intention is to be able to design interfaces that afford the ability to interrogate AI-based models and systems on particular experiential qualities. This is among others, relevant for designers to assess qualities of models ahead of their implementation in a system in the wild.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718871"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics","Generative AI","Postphenomenology","reflexive use"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for reflexive use of generative ai","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://studiolab.ide.tudelft.nl/studiolab/genai-dis2023/files/2023/07/Designing-for-reflexive-use_Christian_Sivertsen-1.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718871","ids":["itu-76c2ec1f-41ff-4ac2-af6e-0b264bfd3ed3"],"keyword":["aesthetics","generative ai","postphenomenology","reflexive use"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F63F689B4A07FF2883061183B3072C9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://studiolab.ide.tudelft.nl/studiolab/genai-dis2023/files/2023/07/Designing-for-reflexive-use_Christian_Sivertsen-1.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-76c2ec1f-41ff-4ac2-af6e-0b264bfd3ed3"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing for Reflexive Use of Generative AI","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718871","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The use of technology in art museums is usually limited to communicating verbal information such as interpretive text and audio guides, or to facilitating social experiences. This paper presents a Research through Design study of an immersive room-scale installation in an art museum. The aim was to afford non-verbal art mediation and educate the attention of museum visitors to certain aspects of a series of paintings. The installation was based on recent art historical research and aimed to use this research to facilitate a new perspective on the artworks. The installation was created through a one-year-long iterative process that involved diverse stakeholder groups of experts, visitors, and non-visitors in testing and formative evaluation. The final design was part of the opening of the new [XX] museum in October 2021 and was visited by almost 80,000 people in four months. Through interviews with 47 visitors, we evaluate how their experience corresponds with the design intent, and how the installation through non-verbal means drew their attention to aspects of the related artwork. We find that the installation largely evokes the intended aesthetic qualities and support reflection on Edvard Munch’s life and artistic practice. Finally, we discuss the use of education of attention as a lens for design practitioners to conceptualize and evaluate how their designs mediate learning and interpretive practices for art museum visitors.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Mathias, Nikita","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718849"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","South Africa"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","MUNCH","University of the Free State"],"keyword":["Art Mediation","Design","Education of Attention","Immersive"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"educating the attention of museum visitors through non verbal art mediation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/iasdr.2023.222","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718849","ids":["itu-45ec16e4-d697-407b-9f94-1aae53f87b27"],"keyword":["Art Mediation","Design","Education of Attention","Immersive"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9676E1BBDDF9C002CBFFE9BEE6B98D8D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/iasdr.2023.222","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.designresearchsociety.org/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1075&context=iasdr","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"munch","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"MUNCH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"za","key":"university of the free state","loc":["South Africa","Africa"],"name":"University of the Free State","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nikita","key":"mathiaspau","last":"Mathias","name":"Mathias, Nikita","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"D","key":"desainzmolestinapedh","last":"De Sainz Molestina","name":"De Sainz Molestina, D","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"L","key":"galluzzopedh","last":"Galluzzo","name":"Galluzzo, L","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"F","key":"rizzopedh","last":"Rizzo","name":"Rizzo, F","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"D","key":"spallazzopedh","last":"Spallazzo","name":"Spallazzo, D","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/iasdr.2023.222","place":"Milan, Italy","status":"p","subtitle":"Life-Changing Design","title":"IASDR 2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-45ec16e4-d697-407b-9f94-1aae53f87b27"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Educating the attention of museum visitors through non-verbal art mediation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718849","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"HCI projects bringing digital and interactive technologies into art museums are affected by a conception of the relation between art and design that narrows the available design space. This is often done by positioning such technologies either as presenting information about artworks, as artworks themselves, or by taking a ’hands-off’ approach. Aiming to re-investigate this conceptual space, we draw on an enactive approach to art developed by Alva Noë and, by means of a design example (an installation in the MUNCH museum), discuss how this approach redirected the design process. Specifically, how it affected the way the design team related to the original artworks and their history, and how they approached evaluating their work. We show by example how understanding such technologies in terms of how they educate visitors’ attention, similarly to art critique, allows designers to participate in correspondence with artworks using unique material, aesthetic, and embodied means.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Smith, Maarten","van der Zwan, Sander"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718899"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology"],"keyword":["Design Process in Interactive Installations","Digital Technologies in Art Museums","Enactive Approach to Art","Human Computer Interaction HCI","Visitor Attention in Museums"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"art critique by other means","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3563657.3596069","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718899","ids":["itu-9e3c8d38-fe0a-4040-9d4f-0d4d6f9b327a"],"keyword":["Design Process in Interactive Installations","Digital Technologies in Art Museums","Enactive Approach to Art","Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)","Visitor Attention in Museums"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7A71D3E9F4649809CA741A5418F950EF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://chrome-extension://efaidnbmnnnibpcajpcglclefindmkaj/https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3563657.3596069","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101310726/art-critique-by-other-means-authors-version.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maarten","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Maarten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sander","key":"vanderzwanpau","last":"van der Zwan","name":"van der Zwan, Sander","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3563657.3596069","eisbn":["9781450398930"],"pages":"343-352","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2023 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference","title":"DIS '23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9e3c8d38-fe0a-4040-9d4f-0d4d6f9b327a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Art Critique by Other Means","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718899","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"he senses are finding their way back into the art museum, but the way paintings are displayed is still constrained by their fragility. We explore whether it would be helpful to use the capabilities of digital technologies to create meaningful somaesthetic experiences with digital reproductions. We conducted an experiment with 19 participants, letting them handle physical paintings and 2D and 3D digital reproductions, while ranking them according to their personal preference. To discover which cultural qualities participants ascribe to artworks in light of their somaesthetic experience, we interviewed participants regarding their experience of ranking three setups. We found that participants regarded the 3D reproductions as having certain material qualities. We argue that by designing the somaesthetic experience of digital reproductions, it might be possible to bring back dimensions of the art experience that were lost with the development of the modern museum.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Sivertsen, Christian","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384791"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Art experience","Post Phenomenology","Somaesthetics","digital reproductions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"handling digital reproductions of artworks","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://somaesthetics.aau.dk/index.php/JOS/article/view/6688/6032","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384791","identifier":[{"id":"85124980598","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ef64fd73-16dc-4dc1-a3ed-b7c2089bf503"],"keyword":["art experience","digital reproductions","post-phenomenology","somaesthetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D3BAC214473058C6D449111299CA7D9A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://somaesthetics.aau.dk/index.php/JOS/article/view/6688/6032","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"sivertsenpau","last":"Sivertsen","locid":"610312cd-b173-4efa-bbb5-0a22e9b9ce02","name":"Sivertsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6843-5009","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","locid":"22ec9269-2fff-4dbf-a9c7-5037559a15ee","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","orcid":"0000-0003-0484-4668","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["22468498"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Somaesthetics","pages":"51-71","publisher":"Aalborg Universitet","status":"p","title":"Journal of Somaesthetics","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ef64fd73-16dc-4dc1-a3ed-b7c2089bf503"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Handling digital reproductions of artworks","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384791","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
